From 3907b42398e689611fefb15454a33b8f440c9bf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavier Ruiz <github@xav.ie>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:27:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Rank tool search by similarity vectors kept in the
 database when EXECUTOR_EMBED_URL is set

The local server passes an OpenAI compatible /v1/embeddings endpoint to the SDK.
Tool search then keeps two tables of its own, created when they are first needed
and outside the versioned schema, so the storage version and the tool search
rows are unchanged and a server that does not know the tables ignores them:
executor_tool_search_texts holds each row's embedding text with the digest of
the tool it was made from, and executor_tool_search_vectors holds real[] unit
vectors keyed by model and text digest. real[] needs no extension on Postgres or
PGlite. An executor without embeddings never creates them.

Writing a listing stays independent of the endpoint. A background fill makes the
text of each current row whose tool changed (purpose first: title, description,
name and input names, then app and router), embeds texts without a vector of the
current model in batches, and drops texts and vectors no row uses. Vectors are
shared by every row with the same text and survive restarts and listing
rewrites; a failed fill is retried by the next write or search.

A search with words embeds only its query (cached, EXECUTOR_EMBED_TIMEOUT_MS,
1500 by default). The page statement then ranks items by weighted reciprocal
rank fusion of their BM25 rank and cosine rank, keeping scopes, merging across
targets, namespaces, exact paths, totals and the page budget. Items without a
vector rank by BM25; items matching no word rank only among the 50 most similar.
EXECUTOR_EMBED_KEYWORD_WEIGHT sets the word share and defaults to 0, which
ranked recorded searches best. Without the endpoint, or when the query embedding
fails, search runs the BM25 statement unchanged.
